# Repository overview

This repo has two primary projects plus root-level domain references:

1. `gtp-telemetry/` — a browser-only React/Vite app that parses local `.ibt` files, analyzes them client-side, and renders a dashboard with PDF export
2. `iracing-gtp-engineer-plugin/` — a Claude plugin/skill package with command docs, a standalone Python IBT parser, and setup-engineering references
3. Root docs — `SKILL.md`, `per-car-quirks.md`, `telemetry-channels.md`, `ibt-parsing-guide.md`

## App architecture

- React 19 + TypeScript + Vite 7 frontend
- Tailwind CSS 4 for styling, Zustand for state, Recharts for charts
- `gtp-telemetry/src/store/session-store.ts` owns the file -> validate -> parse -> analyze pipeline
- `gtp-telemetry/src/lib/ibt-parser.ts` is the browser parser
- `gtp-telemetry/src/lib/analysis-engine.ts` feeds most dashboard and export views
- `gtp-telemetry/src/components/dashboard/` contains chart and analysis panels
- `gtp-telemetry/src/components/shared/` contains reusable UI primitives
- `gtp-telemetry/src/data/car-quirks/` and `src/data/tracks/` hold static domain data

## Plugin architecture

- `iracing-gtp-engineer-plugin/plugin.json` is the manifest (1 skill, 3 commands)
- `iracing-gtp-engineer-plugin/commands/` contains slash-command docs
- `iracing-gtp-engineer-plugin/skills/iracing-gtp-engineer/` is the installed skill source with reference docs
- `iracing-gtp-engineer-plugin/scripts/parse_ibt.py` is the standalone Python parser
- `iracing-gtp-engineer-plugin/install.ps1` must stay in sync with manifest and layout changes

## Expectations

- Treat the telemetry app as a local-first browser app; do not assume a backend or HTTP API exists
- Keep committed config at the repository root unless a subproject is intentionally meant to be opened alone
- Prefer repo-relative paths over machine-specific assumptions
- Avoid hardcoded absolute paths in committed config
- When in doubt about telemetry domain behavior, consult `SKILL.md` and the plugin reference docs before inventing new assumptions
